WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.180
November 2008. The world
is in a financial crisis.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.380
Visiting the London School of Economics,

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.490
Queen Elizabeth the Second
asks why nobody saw it coming.

4
00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.050
Economists can study the same
evidence and still disagree

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.150
about what a government should do.

6
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.060
So when economists disagree,
is it about the evidence,

7
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:22.760
or about values?

8
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:26.020
In this mission, you'll learn
how economists use models,

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.090
assumptions and ceteris
paribus to test ideas.

10
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.690
Then you'll sort
statements about inflation,

11
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.900
taxes and wages into two
very different kinds.

12
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: work out where the
evidence ends and the judgement begins.
